\section*{Bridge Diagnostic}
Before beginning, calculate or explain each item.
\begin{enumerate}
\item Differentiate \(x^4-3x^2+1\).
\item Differentiate \((x^2+1)^5\).
\item Differentiate \(x^2e^x\).
\item Find \(dy/dx\) for \(x^2+y^2=25\).
\item If \(s(t)=t^3-6t\), find \(s'(t)\) and \(s''(t)\).
\item State the units of \(C'(q)\) if \(C\) is dollars and \(q\) is items.
\item Solve \(3x^2-12x+9=0\).
\item Explain why a solution of \(f'(x)=0\) is only a candidate for an extremum.
\end{enumerate}
\begin{bgreveal}
Answers: \(4x^3-6x\); \(10x(x^2+1)^4\); \(e^x(x^2+2x)\); \(-x/y\); \(3t^2-6\), \(6t\); dollars per item; \(x=1,3\); a horizontal tangent can occur without a maximum or minimum, so sign or value tests are still needed.
\end{bgreveal}

Missing more than two computational items suggests a short return to the corresponding Unit 2A review page. Application work becomes much easier when differentiation itself is no longer consuming all available attention.
